THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
====================

OpenFAST and the NREL 5MW / OC4 jacket reference model
------------------------------------------------------
This project analyses the NREL 5MW reference turbine on the OC4 jacket
substructure, simulated with OpenFAST. Those model files -- the .fst glue
file, the ElastoDyn / AeroDyn / HydroDyn / SeaState / ServoDyn / SubDyn /
InflowWind decks, the shared 5MW_Baseline blade, airfoil and controller data,
and the compiled DISCON controller library -- are the work of the National
Renewable Energy Laboratory and its OC4 project partners, not of this
project.

They are published as part of the OpenFAST regression-test suite:

  https://github.com/OpenFAST/r-test

and are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

NONE OF THAT MATERIAL IS REDISTRIBUTED IN THIS REPOSITORY.

Every deck this project consumes was verified to be byte-identical to its
upstream r-test copy: no NREL file was modified. All of this project's
changes to the model are applied at run time, in code, by
simulation/of_inputs.py -- which is this project's own work and is published
here under CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE).

To obtain the model files, run:

  python scripts/fetch_openfast_inputs.py --clone

which stages them from the pinned upstream commit recorded in
scripts/rtest_manifest.json and verifies each file by SHA-256. The manifest
records the exact commit the published results were produced with, so a
verification failure means your model differs from the one behind the numbers
in results/.


Standards referenced
--------------------
The methodology implements procedures from DNV-RP-C203, DNV-ST-0126,
EN 1993-1-1 and IEC 61400. Those documents are copyrighted by their
respective publishers and are NOT reproduced here. Where a numerical
parameter is taken from a standard it appears in the source with a clause or
table citation so it can be checked against a licensed copy. Readers need
their own access to the standards to verify the implementation.


Reference and comparison data
-----------------------------
Validation against the OC4 Phase I code-comparison exercise relies on
project deliverables and participant result sets belonging to the OC4
partners. Those documents are not redistributed here; they are cited in the
thesis and should be obtained from their publishers.
